{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 5, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 drama film directed by david finch er, written by greysan crowder, scott neustadter, and vanessa Taylor, and produced by finch er and kevin francia. the film is based on the true story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed.\n\nthe film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, a brilliant and introverted college student who creates thefacebook, a social networking site that quickly gains popularity. the film also features a talented ensemble cast, including andy garcía as eduardo saverin, the co-founder of facebook and mark's best friend; jemaine clemens as christopher buccarino, a rival programmer who helps mark with thefacebook; and brian christian bales as nathan baxter, a graduate student who becomes a key player in facebook's early success.\n\none of the standout aspects of the film is its portrayal of mark zuckerberg's character. eisenberg delivers a nuanced and complex performance, capturing the intensity and vulnerability of the real mark zuckerberg. the film also explores the complexities of mark's relationships with his friends and colleagues, including his romance with cassie frank (jonah hoffman) and his strained relationship with eduardo saverin.\n\nthe film's direction is also noteworthy, with finch er using a combination of intimate and sweeping camera shots to capture the mood and atmosphere of each scene. the film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is equally impressive, using a haunting and pulsing sound to capture the sense of excitement and tension that defines the facebook phenomenon.\n\nthe film's attention to historical detail is also impressive, with the filmmakers taking care to accurately recreate the early days of facebook and the lawsuits that followed. the film's script is also clever and engaging, using humor and satire to poke fun at the excesse